{
  "_comment": [
    "Executed behaviour probes. Each one runs a pinned binary against the materialised fixture",
    "tree and records what actually happened into content/index/behaviors.tsv.",
    "",
    "The `control` field is what makes a probe evidence rather than a coincidence. A pattern that",
    "matches proves only that *something* matched; it cannot distinguish 'the feature works' from",
    "'the pattern happened to match for an unrelated reason'. So a feature probe carries a second",
    "command, identical except for the feature under test, which MUST fail. Both halves must come",
    "out right or the probe records `inconclusive` -- never a pass.",
    "",
    "PCRE2 10.48 is the asserted baseline, checked by build.py before anything here runs, so",
    "`since_pcre2` on a row is history rather than a gate. It is not decoration either: ripgrep's",
    "own `--pcre2-version` reads 10.45 on this machine while the linked library is 10.48, so a",
    "reference that trusted the version string would be three releases wrong.",
    "",
    "`expect` is one of: match | no-match | error | a regex stdout must satisfy.",
    "Exit codes: rg 0=match 1=no-match 2=error. ast-grep run 0=match 1=no-match.",
    "ast-grep outline exits 0 even on an empty outline -- an empty result there is data, not failure."
  ],
  "probes": [
    {
      "id": "P001",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "lookahead",
      "question": "Does the default engine reject lookahead, and does -P accept it?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-P",
        "-c",
        "foo(?= bar)",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "no-match",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-c",
        "foo(?= bar)",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "error",
      "note": "The control is the point: the default engine errors on lookahead rather than silently not matching.",
      "since_pcre2": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "P002",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "lookahead",
      "question": "Does positive lookahead match through -P?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "he(?= said)",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "match",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "he(?= shouted)",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "no-match",
      "since_pcre2": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "P003",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "lookbehind",
      "question": "Does positive lookbehind match through -P?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "(?<=said )\"hello\"",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "match",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "(?<=shouted )\"hello\"",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "no-match",
      "since_pcre2": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "P004",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "variable-lookbehind",
      "question": "Is bounded variable-length lookbehind accepted?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-coP",
        "(?<=.{0,20}said )\\S+",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "match",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-coP",
        "(?<=.*said )\\S+",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "error",
      "note": "Unbounded lookbehind is a compile error; the bound is what makes it legal.",
      "since_pcre2": "10.43"
    },
    {
      "id": "P005",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "backreference",
      "question": "Do numeric backreferences work through -P?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "(\\w+) \\1",
        "docs/notes.md"
      ],
      "expect": "alpha alpha",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-o",
        "(\\w+) \\1",
        "docs/notes.md"
      ],
      "control_expect": "error",
      "since_pcre2": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "P006",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "named-backreference",
      "question": "Do named backreferences work, so paired delimiters can be required?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "(?<q>[\"'])\\w+\\k<q>",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "match",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "(?<q>[\"'])zzzz\\k<q>",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "no-match",
      "since_pcre2": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "P007",
