    },
    {
      "id": "P011",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "conditional",
      "question": "Are conditional patterns accepted?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-coP",
        "(\")?\\w+(?(1)\"|\\b)",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "match",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-co",
        "(\")?\\w+(?(1)\"|\\b)",
        "docs/quotes.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "error",
      "since_pcre2": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "P012",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "recursion",
      "question": "Does whole-pattern recursion match balanced delimiters, and what does the default engine do with the same pattern?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "\\((?:[^()]|(?R))*\\)",
        "docs/nested.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "(a(b)c)",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "--engine=default",
        "-o",
        "\\((?:[^()]|(?R))*\\)",
        "docs/nested.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "match",
      "control_mode": "differs",
      "note": "One of the sharpest traps in this repository. Lookaround fails loudly under the default engine, with an error naming -P. Recursion does NOT: the default engine parses (?R) as an inline group, silently degrades the pattern to \\([^()]*\\), and returns `(b)` where PCRE2 returns `(a(b)c)`. A wrong answer, not an error. Never assume the default engine will tell you that a PCRE2 construct was unsupported.",
      "since_pcre2": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "P013",
      "tool": "rg",
      "topic": "pcre2-advanced-regex",
      "construct": "recursion-returned-captures",
      "question": "Do subroutine calls return selected capture groups to the caller?",
      "command": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "(?(DEFINE)(?<day>(?|(?<s>Sat)urday|(?<s>Sun)day)))(?&day(<s>)),\\k<s>",
        "docs/weekend.txt"
      ],
      "expect": "match",
      "control": [
        "rg",
        "-oP",
        "(?(DEFINE)(?<day>(?|(?<s>Sat)urday|(?<s>Sun)day)))(?&day),\\k<s>",
        "docs/weekend.txt"
      ],
      "control_expect": "no-match",
      "note": "Returned-capture recursion, which upstream introduced in 10.47 (its own docs first said 10.46 and were corrected). Without the returned-capture list the backreference cannot see \\k<s>, so the control must fail -- that pairing is what makes the match evidence rather than a coincidence.",
      "since_pcre2": "10.47"
    },
    {
